      {
        "eligible_for_bounty": true,
        "eligible_for_submission": true,
        "instructions": "Vercel Sandbox lets customers run programs in an isolated environment, take disk snapshots, limit egress network connections, and perform credential brokering at the networking level.\n\nThe Firecracker microVM is the isolation boundary; escaping the container into the guest OS alone does not qualify. In-scope findings include escapes to the underlying host, cross-tenant access on another customer's sandbox, Sandbox firewall bypasses, Vercel-side exposure of brokered credentials, and Sandbox control-plane authentication or authorization flaws.\n\nSee Sandbox-specific architecture, examples, known findings, testing instructions and out of scope exclusions in the attached document.  ",
        "raw": {
          "asset_identifier": "Vercel sandbox",
          "asset_type": "OTHER",
          "availability_requirement": "medium",
          "confidentiality_requirement": "high",
          "eligible_for_bounty": true,
          "eligible_for_submission": true,
          "instruction": "Vercel Sandbox lets customers run programs in an isolated environment, take disk snapshots, limit egress network connections, and perform credential brokering at the networking level.\n\nThe Firecracker microVM is the isolation boundary; escaping the container into the guest OS alone does not qualify. In-scope findings include escapes to the underlying host, cross-tenant access on another customer's sandbox, Sandbox firewall bypasses, Vercel-side exposure of brokered credentials, and Sandbox control-plane authentication or authorization flaws.\n\nSee Sandbox-specific architecture, examples, known findings, testing instructions and out of scope exclusions in the attached document.  ",
